# Phase 0 - Enterprise Planning

## Business Requirements

Aurora CloudSec has experienced significant growth and now employs 45 staff from its Melbourne headquarters.

The existing IT infrastructure has become difficult to manage, lacks standardisation, and cannot easily scale as the company expands.

Management has approved the design and deployment of a new enterprise infrastructure that supports future growth, improves security, and provides a modern hybrid environment capable of integrating with Microsoft cloud services.

The infrastructure must provide:

- Centralised identity management
- Secure authentication
- Reliable networking
- File and print services
- Remote management
- Cloud integration
- Enterprise security
- High availability where appropriate
- A platform that can grow with the business

---

## Project Objectives

This project aims to:

- Design the enterprise before implementation
- Understand why each technology is required
- Deploy infrastructure using industry best practices
- Document every technical and business decision
- Create a portfolio that reflects real-world enterprise administration
